# Contributing to CommandLane Community

Thanks for your interest in contributing to the CommandLane community space.
This repository is for **community resources**, not the core application code.

## Ways you can contribute

- **Share example hooks** and scripts for CommandLane
- **Improve docs**: clarify instructions, fix typos, add FAQs
- **Suggest features** or integrations by filing issues
- **Report problems** with public docs or examples in this repo

If you want to discuss broader product ideas, you can also join the Discord.

- Discord: https://discord.com/channels/1445425782838005992
- Support: support@commandlane.ai

## Before you open an issue

1. **Search existing issues** to see if your question / problem is already tracked.
2. Use clear, descriptive titles.
3. For bugs, please include:
   - What you were trying to do
   - Steps to reproduce (if applicable)
   - What you expected to happen
   - What actually happened

## Before you open a pull request

1. Make sure your change is **scoped and focused**.
2. If you’re not sure about direction, open a short **Discussion** or Issue first.
3. Keep PRs small and self-contained when possible.
4. Follow the existing style of the docs (Markdown headings, tone, code blocks).

### PR checklist

- [ ] The change is clearly explained in the PR description
- [ ] Docs/examples build or render correctly (where applicable)
- [ ] No secrets, credentials, or private code included

## Code of Conduct

By participating in this project, you agree to uphold our
[`CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md`](./CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md). Be respectful, assume good intent,
and keep feedback constructive.

## Security issues

Please **do not** open public issues for security-sensitive reports.
Instead, follow [`SECURITY.md`](./SECURITY.md) for responsible disclosure.
